From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 02:54:55 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 41/93] arm64: dts: apple: t6050: give the G17C OPP tables
 schema-valid names

opp-v2-base.yaml allows one suffix after opp-table, so
opp-table-gpu-afr and opp-table-gpu-cs fail CHECK_DTBS. J716c already
carried those warnings; sharing the block with J714c and K116c would
add the same four on each board. Rename the nodes to opp-table-afr and
opp-table-cs. Nothing looks them up by name: drm/asahi and the loader
follow the GPU node's apple,afr-opp and apple,cs-opp phandles.

Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <address-in-upstream-commit@localhost>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-gpu-g17c.dtsi | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-gpu-g17c.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-gpu-g17c.dtsi
index a7841f66693..4fc4df0789b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-gpu-g17c.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t6050-gpu-g17c.dtsi
@@ -151,7 +151,7 @@ opp13 {
 		};
 	};
 
-	gpu_afr_opp: opp-table-gpu-afr {
+	gpu_afr_opp: opp-table-afr {
 		compatible = "operating-points-v2";
 
 		opp00 {
@@ -225,7 +225,7 @@ opp13 {
 		};
 	};
 
-	gpu_cs_opp: opp-table-gpu-cs {
+	gpu_cs_opp: opp-table-cs {
 		compatible = "operating-points-v2";
 
 		opp00 {
